// Phase 1 item 3, 3순위 prep (graphMaxCells re-tuning, see CLAUDE.md section
// 2.16(a)/2.17): 700x700x1 grid (490,000 cells, just below graphMaxCells=
// 500000), adaptive dt (FixDt unset), default solver (RK45DP, no setsolver()
// call), baseline (no CUDA Graph). Same config as _graph_poc_700_rk45dp.mx3,
// but using steps() for the measured run.
//
// IMPORTANT: 490,000 cells is below graphMaxCells=500000, so since the
// "Run()/Steps() transparent integration" (CLAUDE.md 2.16(a)), a plain
// steps(100) here would ALSO be silently routed through tryRunGraph() and
// give the same (graph) throughput as _graph_poc_700_rk45dp.mx3 -- making
// this script useless as a "nograph" baseline. To force the genuine
// non-graph RunWhile() path regardless of graphMaxCells, we add a no-op
// custom field term (zero vector, contributes nothing to B_eff/m) via
// AddFieldTerm(ConstVector(0,0,0)): this makes len(customTerms)!=0, so
// graphIncompatibilityReason() rejects it and Steps() falls back to
// RunWhile(). This adds one extra (cheap) custom-field kernel call per
// torqueFn evaluation -- a small, constant overhead applied identically to
// all _nograph variants in this 3순위-prep batch, so graph/nograph ratios
// remain valid even if absolute S_PER_STEP differs slightly from the
// customTerms-free baselines in section 2.15.
AddFieldTerm(ConstVector(0, 0, 0))

SetGridSize(700, 700, 1)
c := 4e-9
SetCellSize(c, c, c)

msat  = 800e3
aex   = 13e-12
alpha = 0.01
b_ext = vector(0, 0.01, 0)

m = uniform(1, 0, 0)
steps(5) // warm-up: kernel JIT load, FFT plan creation, buffer allocation

m = uniform(1, 0, 0)
t = 0
neval0 := Neval.get()
start := now()
steps(100)
wall := since(start).Seconds()
nevl := Neval.get() - neval0

print("GRIDSIZE:", 700, "x", 700, "x", 1)
print("STEPS:", nevl)
print("WALLTIME_S:", wall)
print("CELLS_PER_S:", 700*700*1*nevl/wall)
print("S_PER_STEP:", wall/nevl)
